Relations: Graph

Purpose:
  Defines standard relation types for the knowledge graph.

RelationTypes:
  CREATED_BY:
    Description: Node was created by another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> CREATED_BY PROMPT-<ID>
  IMPLEMENTS:
    Description: Node implements another node
    Example: CODE-<MODULE>-<ARTIFACT> IMPLEMENTS TASK-<ID>
  DEPENDS_ON:
    Description: Node depends on another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> DEPENDS_ON TASK-<ID>
  BLOCKED_BY:
    Description: Node is blocked by another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> BLOCKED_BY SEC-<ID>
  USES:
    Description: Node uses another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> USES SKILL-<ID>
  TESTED_BY:
    Description: Node is tested by another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> TESTED_BY TEST-<ID>
  VERIFIED_BY:
    Description: Node is verified by another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> VERIFIED_BY TEST-<ID>
  SECURED_BY:
    Description: Node is secured by another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> SECURED_BY SEC-<ID>
  DEPLOYED_BY:
    Description: Node is deployed by another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> DEPLOYED_BY DEPLOY-<ID>
  RUNS_ON:
    Description: Node runs on another node
    Example: API RUNS_ON INFRA-<ID>
  DOCUMENTED_BY:
    Description: Node is documented by another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> DOCUMENTED_BY DOC-<ID>
  CAUSED_BY:
    Description: Node was caused by another node
    Example: INC-<ID> CAUSED_BY TASK-<ID>
  AFFECTS:
    Description: Node affects another node
    Example: INC-<ID> AFFECTS <DOMAIN>
  OWNS:
    Description: Node owns another node
    Example: <LAYER> OWNS TASK-<ID>
  RELATED_TO:
    Description: Node is related to another node
    Example: TASK-<ID> RELATED_TO TASK-<ID>
  REPLACES:
    Description: Node replaces another node
    Example: CODE-<NEW> REPLACES CODE-<OLD>
  SUPERSEDES:
    Description: Node supersedes another node
    Example: DEC-<NEW> SUPERSEDES DEC-<OLD>
  CONFLICTS_WITH:
    Description: Node conflicts with another node
    Example: DEC-<ID> CONFLICTS_WITH <NODE>

RelationRules:
  [RL1]  Relations MUST be directional.
  [RL2]  Relations MUST use standard types.
  [RL3]  Multiple relations between nodes are allowed.
  [RL4]  Relations enable forward and reverse traversal.

State: +
  